en:{
brand_name:"Starlight Academy · 星光学堂",brand_sub:"Guided by starlight · Science Tutoring · Canada & Worldwide",nav_philosophy:"Our Founding Intention",nav_subjects:"Subjects",nav_teachers:"Teachers",nav_schedule:"Availability",nav_contact:"Contact",nav_book:"Book a session →",
hero_eyebrow:"Little points of starlight · a guiding light",hero_title:"Guided by starlight,<br>find the way you learn best.",hero_lead:"Starlight Academy — science tutoring for high school (Secondary 4–5) and CEGEP students across Canada, available online worldwide. We do more than explain problems: we guide each student to find the learning method that suits them best, and through continuous learning, to find the path to realizing their own value. Taught in our spare time by our three founders — Simon, Ivy and Johnny — on weekday evenings and weekends, online globally or in person in Montréal.",
philosophy_title:"Our Founding Intention · Guided by Starlight",philosophy_quote:"“Our original intention is to <em>guide each student to find the learning method that suits them best</em>, and through continuous learning, to find the <em>path and way to realize their own value</em>.”",philosophy_p:"Every student is a point of starlight — with their own pace, starting point and way of shining. Starlight does not force everyone into the same method: we first help you see how you learn most effectively, then walk the road steadily with you, step by step, with scientific logic and patience. Grades are a result; finding your method and direction is the light you carry for life.",philosophy_story:"Starlight Academy was founded by three passionate university students. We are still in classes and still learning ourselves, yet we genuinely want to help others — so we use our spare time outside classes, on evenings and weekends, to learn alongside our students. We believe that spending our time helping others grow is itself a way of creating value; and when a student finds their method and begins to shine, little by little, we are realizing our own value too.",
phil1_t:"✦ Find your way",phil1_p:"We first look at your habits and sticking points, then set your pace: some learn through diagrams and experiments, some through derivations, some through lots of worked examples — when the method fits, effort counts.",
phil2_t:"✦ Grow by continuing",phil2_p:"Learning is not a one-time sprint, but steady accumulation. Each lesson leaves clear practice and a next goal, so progress is visible and lasting.",
phil3_t:"✦ Toward your own value",phil3_p:"Science is more than grades. It trains thinking, problem-solving and persistence — abilities that will help you, in studies and in life, find the path to realizing your own value.",
subj_physics:"Physics",subj_chem:"Chemistry",subj_bio:"Biology",subj_calc:"Calculus",
scope1:"🇨🇦 Across Canada",scope2:"🌍 Online worldwide",scope3:"📍 In person in Montréal",btn_book:"Book a session",btn_schedule:"See availability ↓",
hero_hours:"<strong>Class times</strong> · Weekdays (Mon–Fri) <strong>after 18:00</strong> &nbsp;|&nbsp; Sat–Sun <strong>daytime + evening</strong>",
hero_founders:"All three teachers are founders and teach all subjects — Simon (Electrical Engineering, McGill), Ivy (biology-related program), Johnny (Biochemistry, McGill).",
about_title:"About Starlight Academy",about_sub:"Starlight Academy is a science tutoring team founded by three passionate university students, serving students across Canada and online worldwide. No large lecture classes — only one-on-one or small-group tutoring: we find exactly where you are stuck at school and how you learn best, then rebuild the concepts, worked examples and exam question types step by step for your curriculum.",
about1_t:"🎯 Aligned to your curriculum",about1_p:"Aligned to Québec Secondary Science, SN Math and CEGEP science syllabi, and adaptable to other provincial curricula. Practice maps directly to school quizzes and final exams.",
about2_t:"🗣️ Trilingual support",about2_p:"Lessons and communication in Chinese, English or French, switching languages when a concept is tricky — ideal if you study in English or French and want the terminology to truly make sense.",
about3_t:"🌍 Across Canada · Online worldwide",about3_p:"Online lessons have no borders: book from any Canadian province, or from abroad on Montréal time (ET). In-person sessions are available in Montréal. After each lesson you get clear practice and a goal for next time, and parents can follow up by email anytime.",
subjects_title:"Subjects · Four Canadian sciences",subjects_sub:"All four subjects cover Canadian high school and CEGEP levels, and online students worldwide can book the same content. Each founder teaches all four subjects — mix and match teacher and subject freely when you book.",
phys_p:"Secondary 5 Physics, CEGEP Mechanics (203-NYA), Electricity & Magnetism, Waves & Optics. Force analysis, electric and magnetic fields, and lab-style questions.",
chem_p:"Secondary 5 Chemistry, CEGEP General Chemistry (202-NYA) and Chemistry of Solutions. Mole calculations, acids and bases, equilibrium, and lab reports.",
bio_p:"High school Science (biology), CEGEP General Biology I / II (101-NYA, etc.). Cells, genetics and human systems — concept maps plus exam answer technique.",
calc_p:"Secondary 5 SN Math bridging, CEGEP Calculus I (201-NYA) and Calculus II. Limits, derivatives, integrals and applied problems, with a head start for university.",
teachers_title:"Our teachers · 3 founders",teachers_sub:"All three teachers are founders. Each teaches Physics, Chemistry, Biology and Calculus, with the same availability: weekdays after 18:00, and daytime + evenings on weekends.",
role_founder:"Co-founder",
